11. In the case of Sarla Verma (Smt) & Ors. v. Delhi Transport Corporation &Anr.,
(2009) 6 SCC 121, it has been held that where the deceased was married, the deduction towards personal and living expenses of the deceased should be one-third (1/3rd) where the number of dependent family members is between 2 and 3;
one-fourth (1/4th) where the number of dependent family members is between 4 and 6, and one-fifth (1/5th) where the number of dependent family members exceeds six.

18. The Loss of dependency is thus, re- calculated as :-
i) Rs. 10,686 + 40% (towards future prospects) of Rs. 10,686 = Rs. 14960;
ii) Rs. 14960 - Rs. 4986 (i.e. 1/3rd deductions towards personal expenses) = Rs.
9974;
iii) Rs. 9974x12x18 = Rs. 21,54,384/-.
